  "adapter_and_runtime_checks": [
    "Closed source rows and typed SourceSpan records, exact identity-normalized UTF8 selectors, all physical occurrence IDs retained even where prose is equal.",
    "Native384 requires actual native-execution receipt profile, pinned current producer/assets, exact source text plus complete SourceSpan join, untruncated recorded token coverage and finite native float32 unit384 vectors. Injected fixtures, projected8 inputs, width substitutions, missing paragraph/clause records and silent normalization refuse readiness.",
    "Native768 generic cache support is a separate recorded-consistency lane requiring complete bounded production/loading inventories; producer reports lack physical SourceSpan, so text-only producer join and producer_source_span_present=false are retained. It is not exercised or numerically qualified by this pilot.",
    "Both cache inputs and contexts are regenerated from explicit original requests/refs and independently verified source files; modified/resealed caches fail. Row/clauses bounds64/8 and artifact/token bounds remain closed.",
    "Runtime resolver authenticates the plaintext source and returns the local path required by corpus._read_verified. Source documents remain opaque UTF8 bytes; they are not parsed as targets or JSON.",
    "Origin checks at _prepare entry, _source_packet entry, post-cache validation, final preparation, lazy model opening and later rechecks precede the new validation/model boundaries. Exact current owner pins are fenced before/after use; the dynamic 768 profile has an explicit origin check.",
    "Runtime uses the separate new contract ID in capture, plan and describe; original normative owner files and retained assay registration are not changed by this opt-in adapter.",
    "Opening remains lazy and explicit; original selected state, normative32 vocabulary/codec, original TRAIN-only preprocessing/count prior and donor restoration remain fixed. New input readiness does not add actors/actions to the 32-symbol output language."
